{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>Thus</b> — Rabbi Judah HaLevi said: The mem of <b>כִּי</b> [for], the heh of <b>הַזֹּאת</b> [this] is missing, as though it were written <b>הֲגַם</b> [even], <b>בְּעֵינֵיכֶם יִפְלָא</b> [would it be marvelous in your eyes], like <b>אַתָּה תַעֲשֶׂה מְלוּכָה</b> [you will establish kingship] over Israel, which is missing the heh of <b>הַזֹּאת</b>, as though it were <b>הָאַתָּה</b>. In my opinion there is no need, for the verse is not saying that it would be marvelous to Him, for then it would appear punctuated [with a question] like <b>הִמִּמֶּנִּי יִפָּלֵא</b> [would it be marvelous from me?]. Rather here it is written <b>גַּם בְּעֵינֵיכֶם יִפָּלֵא</b> [it will also be marvelous in your eyes], and just as this thing that I am doing is marvelous in the eyes of this people — also in His eyes I have done a great wonder, only <b>בְּעֵינֵיכֶם יִפָּלֵא</b> [it will be marvelous in your eyes], like <b>הִיא נִפְלָאֹת בְּעֵינֵינוּ</b> [it is marvelous in our eyes]. And the meaning is: I will do a wonder such as I have not done the like of. And I have seen a figurative interpretation."], :book :zechariah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {0 "The Hebrew cites partial words and verse fragments; I have rendered them as Ibn Ezra quotes them with their meanings in brackets. The phrase 'אעשה פלא לא עשיתי כמוהו' echoes language reminiscent of Exodus 15:11 but is not a direct citation; translated literally."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Zecharia -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/zecharya"] ["1" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=25&perek=5&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:46:26.691644741Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}